\deftab720
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I think quake-trance should have a very specific musical ancestry: 
\f1\b psytrance that has gone downward instead of faster
\f0\b0 .\
Historically, psytrance already gives you the right DNA: relentless four-on-the-floor pulse, rolling bass, long-form accumulation rather than conventional songs, outdoor all-night culture, and an origin in Goa. Modern progressive psy tends toward the slower, rolling end; forest psy makes texture and the natural environment part of the sound; darkpsy supplies menace and physical intensity. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://timbr.music/blog/psytrance-subgenres?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 TIMBR Radio}}) There is also a real Southern Californian underground desert electronic tradition, while Arcosanti has hosted psychedelic/minimal techno and bass-oriented events in the Arizona desert. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arcosanti.org/revival-of-tradition-arcofest-2023/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Arcosanti}})direct\
That gives you a delicious historical joke: 
\f1\b quake-trance can emerge in the American Southwest as a genre whose practitioners have forgotten that one of its remote musical ancestors came from Goa\'97and centuries later the Order triumphantly \'93discovers\'94 Goa and takes it home.
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 What quake-trance sounds like\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 I wouldn't make it a descendant of hi-tech psy. Hi-tech gets its extremity by accelerating towards 180\'96200+ BPM. Quake-trance should discover that 
\f1\b speed is spiritually vulgar
\f0\b0 .\
Its founders realise that the important part of a rave is the bit below hearing.\
Early quake-trance probably starts around 
\f1\b 128\'96138 BPM
\f0\b0 , descended from progressive psy and darker psychedelic techno. The audible kick remains recognisably trance-like, but underneath it is an engineered infrasonic structure produced by the Gyges discs.\
So there are really 
\f1\b two tempos
\f0\b0 .\
The dancers hear perhaps 132 BPM.\
The landscape hears something like 4.125 Hz, 8.25 Hz, 16.5 Hz and a collection of uglier subharmonics that cause geological survey equipment to request compassionate leave.\
This becomes one of the genre's defining aesthetic principles:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 The people dance to the beat. The earth dances to the remainder.
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
A conventional quake-trance track might begin almost disappointingly sparse: kick, rolling bass, little dry percussion, a few psychedelic noises. Over fifteen or twenty minutes, low-frequency structures accumulate beneath it. The audience gradually begins feeling the music through feet, ribs and teeth.\
Eventually the environment starts supplying percussion.\
Dust falls.\
Loose stones chatter.\
Tent poles hum.\
Someone's camper van acquires a rhythm section.\
At that point the DJ has achieved 
\f1\b Drop
\f0\b0 .\
Importantly, 
\f3\i the Drop
\f0\i0  in quake-trance does 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  mean the EDM moment where the bass comes crashing back.\
The Drop is the moment when the surroundings begin participating.\
A mediocre Drop moves the dance floor.\
A good Drop moves the campsite.\
An exceptional Drop gets mentioned by the Geological Survey.\
That distinction would matter enormously to devotees.\
There would be contemptuous genre arguments:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 club quake
\f0\b0  \'97 fake; the building is designed to vibrate.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 festival quake
\f0\b0  \'97 acceptable for beginners.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 canyon quake
\f0\b0  \'97 orthodox.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 tectonic quake
\f0\b0  \'97 advanced and frequently uninsured.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 wet quake
\f0\b0  \'97 initially regarded as decadent Goa nonsense.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 recorded quake
\f0\b0  \'97 theological contradiction. If the geology isn't live, neither is Ludwig.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 Forest psy contributes a lot aesthetically. It already uses organic, environmental and field-recording textures. Quake-trance takes the obvious theological next step: 
\f1\b why sample the environment when you can make the environment perform?
\f0\b0 ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://timbr.music/blog/psytrance-subgenres?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 TIMBR Radio}})\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 How it emerges\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 I would make its origin pleasingly accidental.\
Somewhere around the 
\f1\b late twenty-eighth or early twenty-ninth century
\f0\b0 , cheap obsolete stasis hardware starts appearing in the American Southwest.\
Not complete refrigeration units. Those are useful.\
The unwanted pieces are older industrial Gyges assemblies with obsolete containment systems, warped housings and control interfaces nobody has maintained since the manufacturer was absorbed by a company which was itself absorbed by a pension fund.\
Desert artists love them.\
Initially they are used because spinning Gyges discs produce extraordinary low-frequency effects.\
Someone in the Joshua Tree underground discovers that if you spin one beside a sound system, you can 
\f3\i feel
\f0\i0  something below the bass.\
This is immediately described as spiritual.\
Someone else observes that it is actually mechanical resonance.\
They are asked to leave.\
The first important accident occurs at an outdoor party where two salvaged units are running simultaneously.\
The DJ is midway through an extremely long progressive-psy set. One unit drifts fractionally out of its intended operating regime.\
Then the second does.\
Nothing dramatic happens.\
A sandstone wall about eighty metres away begins humming.\
That is much more important.\
Everyone stops dancing.\
The DJ, displaying the instincts necessary to found a religion, 
\f1\b doesn't stop the music
\f0\b0 .\
He adjusts the tempo.\
The humming grows louder.\
People put their hands against the rock.\
The rock answers through their palms.\
Someone later claims the whole canyon was breathing.\
Someone else claims the canyon said 
\f1\b Ludwig
\f0\b0 .\
Nobody can remember who said it first.\
Within six months there are T-shirts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Why the Southwest?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 The Southwest is nearly perfect, for several independent reasons.\
First, 
\f1\b dry rock is legible
\f0\b0 .\
In saturated ground, energy disappears into complicated coupled systems\'97which is exactly what will later make Goa catastrophically interesting. In a dry canyon, effects are immediate and theatrical. A cliff face vibrates. Pebbles dance. Dust falls from a fissure. Everyone can see that 
\f3\i something happened
\f0\i0 .\
Second, canyon geometry makes the early genre spectacular. You have long exposed surfaces, enclosed basins and natural amphitheatres. Joshua Tree already has the visual grammar you want: enormous boulders, stark open desert, night sky and live music tucked against exposed rock.\
{\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename TyGh9VbRUAYbQw0RCZUNpEfdmSbwnCHJavB5-mYpmscdk6bfm1ralvdI7vR8bsJYcefD77cQJW_hHBZ7i1nCkJ38qsy4O3jB2N4aNrWcxM_Kpp6iwE9mWlgOx7_81oabFT3KlkpAQwrH4dh6-CeoI8lH_QByMf_paGI039n3wf0afsTGcAydVtELo2p82jpe}\picw900\pich720\picwgoal18000\pichgoal14400\jpegblip }}\
{\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename p_HHT0M0uK5GBRBp1xQ3okCY-flMpk4DwLA01xbriGVTEoOfzzLqoSZongQfVQnUt0MvyAnHiKuHf7PZP-CM_9MHO7XO0o6SlkgWJZVIBBVXPiQANtRkehv9TIgumeOdbwvSo3RlTXoOVd8OyGecdwKAM1ZeZqHWaykZSKdz_H_TgijA3aZumAQQClWHqkpI}\picw2048\pich1152\picwgoal40960\pichgoal23040\jpegblip }}\
Third, the desert offers 
\f1\b distance from regulators and neighbours
\f0\b0 , two groups who tend to object when the bass line registers on seismographs.\
Fourth, there is the cultural lineage. Southern California already has underground desert electronic-music culture; Slab City has long attracted people deliberately living outside ordinary institutional structures. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slab_City%2C_California?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Wikipedia}}) In your future, that can mutate over centuries into a semi-mythic tradition of desert congregations, illegal sound systems and discarded industrial technology.\
And fifth, the desert contains a great deal of land whose principal commercial advantage is that 
\f1\b when something goes catastrophically wrong, fewer lawyers can hear it
\f0\b0 .\
That surely matters to early quake-trance promoters.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Where is its birthplace?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 I would give quake-trance 
\f1\b three competing holy places
\f0\b0 , because religions are always improved by a disputed birthplace.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Joshua Tree / Yucca Valley / Twentynine Palms \'97 the popular claim\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 This should be the place ordinary devotees think quake-trance began.\
The 
\f1\b Morongo Basin
\f0\b0  gives you:\
Joshua Tree mysticism; Yucca Valley artists and cheap industrial spaces; Twentynine Palms military residue, scrapyards and access to equipment nobody is entirely certain was decommissioned properly.\
The foundational party could happen in an abandoned quarry or dry canyon somewhere beyond Twentynine Palms.\
Later devotees call it 
\f1\b The First Drop
\f0\b0 .\
Nobody knows the exact site because the original invitation said:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f4\fs20 DRIVE EAST UNTIL YOUR NAV SAYS, \'93ROAD ENDS IN -10 MILES.\'94
\f0\fs24 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u8232 \strokec2 TURN LEFT AT THE BURNT SOFA.\strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f0 Every subsequent generation identifies a different burnt sofa.\
By 3012 there may be 
\f1\b seven competing First Drop canyons
\f0\b0 , all charging admission.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Slab City / Niland \'97 the heretical claim\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Slab City is even better for the engineering side: an off-grid desert community built around remnants of an old military installation. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slab_City%2C_California?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Wikipedia}})\
The Slabbers insist Joshua Tree merely 
\f1\b popularised
\f0\b0  quake-trance.\
According to them, the real invention happened when a technician called 
\f1\b Manny No-Last-Name
\f0\b0  wired a stolen Gyges regulator into a bass stack because he needed \'93more bottom\'94.\
Manny is later canonised.\
The Order denies this because its foundational scriptures require Manny to have been three people.\
The Slab City school retains a rawer form of the music called 
\f1\b slab quake
\f0\b0 , in which technical competence is regarded as commercialism.\
Equipment must look dangerous.\
Exposed cables are doctrinal.\
An intact safety housing is grounds for suspicion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Arcosanti \'97 the intellectual claim\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Arcosanti is wonderful as the place where quake-trance gets 
\f1\b theory
\f0\b0 .\
Its real architecture already has the combination of experimental desert urbanism, concrete vaults and performance spaces that makes this visually plausible. ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arcosanti.org/revival-of-tradition-arcofest-2023/?utm_source=chatgpt.com"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Arcosanti}})\
{\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename acjbG04eaGYja-cuIfFQDaRh8rOOriRgQFaY1AgGWmU21Mna89h32g91hUUlcFiTXJxyfp3r9oT0wjbWr8vBi66i8LhHW76-zDHXyis9Hc1i3IAE2JqG8AKR8y6ssPfQ7AWLYIqGTyqy57Q5qmmUGRsVt74HaBlTpZkdVIEjD6vSEpoZDF3i650ouSKiMtZ8}\picw1200\pich900\picwgoal24000\pichgoal18000\jpegblip }}\
{\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename i6OBvHjC1R9lXsqA8QjS_l9L-mF0HKdPdYCLs8pmzMc8f9vd6R2xQQBGLE_yWrO7_nNPqLevczZYXI9VhQMEnCobM-8xIXrC6lYT6IFL7bQhrTeFtTDQwyRoWuNexLkCnv6p5IjYPTLcj-NKM_K6anbZhWtVI3OimUypeckZ8ej4XMIN5WEIrGUUj_XOYRM7}\picw2000\pich1339\picwgoal40000\pichgoal26780\jpegblip }}\
{\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename X0ax4YmitEGpsUpuf4fHzAOH4VHWo72b3sLvsWscf43hL88rrDSgmIxhtYoZEPPADc1wL1x3q6PcypWSbeM_fuGo9QSP5k-MEJPA7FMSxUKMkfgLQAeUc0JGVMm4ZCR28n1CqtQZV3IOanwajahXb9_WdTQRqhHByoiIOUmyIsK8QqOCXW6cH2JC1H0WVTX7}\picw2048\pich1364\picwgoal40960\pichgoal27280\jpegblip }}\
Perhaps the raw desert scene starts in California, then somebody at Arcosanti notices that the observed environmental responses correspond to 
\f1\b standing-wave geometry
\f0\b0 .\
This is where the first deliberate canyon-scale Drop is engineered.\
Joshua Tree gives quake-trance its soul.\
Slab City claims to have given it its balls.\
Arcosanti gives it equations.\
Everybody hates Arcosanti.\
Particularly after Arcosanti musicians begin referring to themselves as 
\f1\b geo-composers
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 The gods\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 This is where I'd make the history much richer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Ludwig, Zildjian and Rickenbacker are ancient musical brand names whose original meanings have been lost.
\f0\b0 \
Ludwig: drums.\
Zildjian: cymbals.\
Rickenbacker: guitars and basses.\
Pearl: drums.\
Gibson and H\'f6fner: guitars/basses.\
After the 
\f1\b Great Silicon Meltdown
\f0\b0 , enormous portions of American cultural history vanish. But physical objects survive.\
Drum kits survive.\
Cymbals survive.\
Guitars survive.\
Road cases survive.\
Logos survive.\
People several centuries later know that these names were 
\f1\b associated with music
\f0\b0 , but the documentary chain explaining 
\f3\i how
\f0\i0  becomes fragmentary.\
This is precisely the kind of evidentiary environment in which a religion can get some work done.\
An archaeomusicologist finds multiple ancient ritual objects bearing the names:\

\f1\b LUDWIG
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b ZILDJIAN
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b RICKENBACKER
\f0\b0 \
They occur repeatedly in old images of ecstatic gatherings where thousands of people face illuminated platforms while figures manipulate sacred electrical apparatus.\
Which is, objectively, what a concert photograph looks like if you have forgotten concerts.\
Someone proposes that these were manufacturers.\
This theory is dismissed as reductive.\
The theological interpretation becomes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Ludwig \'97 God of the First Impact\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Ludwig governs 
\f1\b impact, pulse, thunder and the initiation of resonance
\f0\b0 .\
His symbol is the circle within a circle: the bass drum.\
He is invoked through the kick.\
Orthodox quake-trance begins with Ludwig because vibration must first be 
\f1\b struck into existence
\f0\b0 .\
His priesthood are percussionists.\
They are called 
\f1\b Luddites
\f0\b0 , which causes endless confusion in surviving historical databases.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Zildjian \'97 God of the Breaking Sky\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Zildjian governs 
\f1\b high-frequency chaos, fracture, metallic violence and revelation
\f0\b0 .\
The great cymbal logos survive on ancient bronze discs, which eventually acquire the status of devotional plates.\
Zildjian is believed to speak when a stable resonance breaks into something new.\
His great theological contribution is the 
\f1\b Crash
\f0\b0 .\
A major Drop may begin under Ludwig and achieve communion with Rickenbacker, but Zildjian is the god who announces that matters have exceeded the insurance policy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Rickenbacker \'97 God Beneath\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f0 Rickenbacker is the most important god to quake-trance.\
Ancient photographs repeatedly associate the name with long-necked electrical instruments, particularly basses.\
Hence Rickenbacker becomes god of:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 low frequencies, buried things, subterranean communication, distant sympathetic vibration and anything felt before it is heard.
\f0\b0 \
The Order believes Rickenbacker lives beneath the crust.\
This creates an obvious theological explanation for remote resonance:\
Rickenbacker does not move through ordinary space.\

\f1\b He is already underneath both places.
\f0\b0 \
The physicists hate this explanation because, irritatingly, it predicts some observations about as well as their own equations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Why those three became principal gods\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 Because quake-trance itself naturally divides into three domains:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Ludwig supplies the beat.
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b Zildjian supplies the rupture.
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b Rickenbacker supplies the resonance.
\f0\b0 \
That gives the religion an actual musical cosmology.\
A Drop progresses through theological stages:\

\f1\b The Calling of Ludwig
\f0\b0  \'97 establish the pulse.\

\f1\b The Opening of Zildjian
\f0\b0  \'97 add increasingly unstable upper harmonics.\

\f1\b The Descent to Rickenbacker
\f0\b0  \'97 bring the Gyges subharmonics into coherence with the landscape.\
Then:\

\f1\b The Perpetual Drop
\f0\b0  \'97 the point at which the musicians cease to be the only participants and the environment joins the composition.\
The Drop is \'93perpetual\'94 because Rickenbacker's vibration theoretically continues forever, propagating beneath the world even after human ears lose it.\
Unfortunately, Rotherhithe will eventually provide disturbing experimental support for this doctrine.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 And the minor gods\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 Pearl, Gibson and H\'f6fner should once have been major gods.\
Theology changes with musical fashion.\
This gives you centuries of ridiculous schisms.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Pearl
\f0\b0  was once Ludwig's principal rival, causing the 
\f1\b Great Drum Schism
\f0\b0 , whose doctrinal difference cannot now be reconstructed because both sides apparently believed in drums.\

\f1\b Gibson
\f0\b0  governs heroic display, excess and solos. This makes him important to an older form of quake-trance featuring more audible guitar.\

\f1\b H\'f6fner
\f0\b0  becomes associated with lightness, levitation and improbable bass frequencies because surviving iconography shows an oddly shaped violin bass in the hands of an enormously revered ancient saint whose identity has been lost.\
By the time of the Order of the Perpetual Drop, these gods are embarrassingly old-fashioned.\
Hence:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 Pearl, Gibson and H\'f6fner were so last Hootenanny.
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
And 
\f1\b Hootenanny
\f0\b0  itself can be a word whose meaning the religion no longer knows.\
They agree it was an ancient ceremony.\
They disagree whether it involved dancing, animal sacrifice, communal singing or competitive knitwear.\
This is the word Hayley searches and fails to recover because the Silicon Meltdown erased most Americana.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 How the religion grows out of the music\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f0 I wouldn't have the Order appear immediately.\
First there is just a genre.\
Then a scene.\
Then scene mythology.\
Then irony.\
Then people who fail to understand that the irony is irony.\
This is how many excellent religions presumably begin.\
Early DJs say things like:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \'93Rickenbacker is awake tonight.\'94\strokec2 \
They mean the sub-bass is working.\
Or:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \'93Ludwig wants another one.\'94\strokec2 \
Meaning the crowd wants another track.\
When a canyon wall responds:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 \'93Zildjian approves.\'94\strokec2 \
Everybody laughs.\
Twenty years later, people are still saying it.\
Fifty years later somebody writes the sayings down.\
